      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a $3\\times 1$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- The matrix $L$ has $3$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 1.$ $\\,\\checkmark$\n\n- The matrix $M$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times$\n\n- The matrix $N$ has $3$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 1.$ $\\,\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, only $L$ and $N$ are $3\\times 1$ matrices.",
